> The semantic versioning spec outlines a standardized versioning system for software
  releases. It provides a consistent way for developers to give a meaning to their
  software releases (how big of a change is this release??)

> Version consists of three numbers separated by periods.

  1.Major Release

  2.Minor Release

  3.Patch Release

> Initial Release

  Typically, first release is 1.0.0

> Patch Releases

  Patch releases normally do not contain new features or significant change.
  They typically signify bug fixes and other changes that do not impact
  how the code is used

> Minor Release

  Minor release signify that new feature or functionality have been added ,
  but the project still in backward compatible. No breaking changes.
  The new functionality is optional and should not force user to rewrite their own
  code.


